# FAQ — canned answers to common client questions

Living document; add new Q&As as they come up. When a client asks one of these,
reproduce the answer closely, personalizing lightly.

**Do you need a meet and greet?**
Meet & greet is optional with me. However if you'd like we can set one up!

**Can we do a meet and greet?**
Absolutely, we can meet at the Brownie Neighborhood Park (Google link: [YOUR MEET-AND-GREET LOCATION LINK]). I'll bring Brownie so the two pups can meet each other and get used to one another's scent. What does your availability look like for the next 7 days? What time frame are you available generally?

**If they insist on doing it at my place:**
Sure! You can bring your pup over. My address is [YOUR ADDRESS], and for the introduction I would take your pup inside by myself first. Assuming everything goes well I'll bring both my pup & yours out so you get to see how they get along as well. Does that process work for you?

**My dog's not neutered/spayed, is that ok?**
Yes! As long as they are not aggressive, Brownie gets along with everyone!!

**I have a puppy and they're really young and haven't finished all their vaccines — can you board them?**
Definitely. I have a lot of experience taking care of young puppies. As far as vaccination goes, since your dog will only be in contact with my dog and my dog is up to date on all of her vaccines, I don't see any issue there.

**I would like to do a video call, can we do that?**
Sure! What time today works for you?

## About me, Brownie & my home

**Will there be other dogs there? / How many dogs do you board at a time?**
I only sit one dog (or one family's pups) at a time! It'll just be your pup and my own pup, Brownie.

**Do you have a dog? Is she friendly?**
I do have a dog! Her name is Brownie and she's a border collie mix. She's super friendly with any non-aggressive dog and loves playing fetch 🤩 She's spayed & fully up to date on all her shots.

**Do you have any other pets, like cats?**
Just Brownie, my dog!

**Where are you located? / What part of town are you in?**
I'm at [YOUR ADDRESS], in the [YOUR NEIGHBORHOOD, e.g. "X area, about 10 min north of Y"].

**Is it a house or an apartment? Do you have a yard?**
I live in a house with a private, fenced backyard! Your pup will be hanging out with me & Brownie.

**Do you have roommates?**
[YOUR HOUSEHOLD, e.g. "No roommates! It's just me living in the house."]

**How much experience do you have?**
I've taken care of 200+ dogs so far & have plenty of experience with puppies too!

**Can I see your home? Can you send photos or a video?**
Of course! I'm happy to send photos or a video walk-through of the house, or hop on a live video call - whatever works best for you!

## Day-to-day during the stay

**Will you be home with my dog? How long are you usually away?**
I'm home most of the time! If I step out it's usually 2-3 hours max, and I have cameras set up in the house so I can always see what's happening.

**Do you crate dogs? Should I bring my crate?**
Crate's not a requirement! I only use it if it's part of your pup's routine. When I'm home they get access to the whole house to roam & explore. If your pup is crate trained, no need to bring yours - I have crates in every size (up to XXL)!

**Where will my dog sleep? Can they sleep on the bed?**
Most pups sleep in the bedroom with me & Brownie! They're welcome on my bed too if that's what they're used to.

**Do you allow dogs on furniture?**
I do allow them on furniture! Do you have a preference on that for your pup?

**Will my dog be left outside? I'm worried about the heat.**
I never leave any dog outside unsupervised - yard time is always monitored. With this heat I keep outdoor play to about 15 min at a time with breaks indoors, plus longer play early morning & late evening.

**What does a typical day look like? How much exercise will my dog get?**
Happy to walk you through it! A ~20-min walk early morning (7-9a) while it's still cool, breakfast around 9-10a, then at least 30 min of fetch in the backyard w water breaks. Dinner is between 6-7p, and another ~20-min walk around sunset to wind the day down. Plenty of cuddle time in between! 🤩 If your pup is used to more activity, just lmk & I'll give them longer walks & more fetch time.

**Will my dog go to a dog park?**
Nope, no dog parks! They'll just hang out here with me & Brownie.

**How often will you send updates?**
I send at least one photo update a day, and more anytime you text & ask! Happy to send a few extra the first day or two so u know they're settling in.

**Are you comfortable giving medication?**
I am comfortable giving medication! Just text me the dose & schedule and I'll note it on my end.

**My dog is a picky eater / might not eat much at first.**
No worries, that's totally normal! A lot of pups don't eat much their first night in a new place. I'll keep an eye on it & keep u updated.

**My dog has some separation anxiety / gets nervous the first day.**
No problem on my end! Most pups settle in within the first day, and having Brownie around usually helps a lot. I'm happy to send extra updates the first couple days for peace of mind.

## Dog-specific questions

**My dog sometimes marks / lifts his leg around other male dogs.**
I'm totally comfortable with it, it's very common!

**My puppy is teething and a bit nippy - is that ok?**
Yes! I have experience with teething puppies and am comfortable monitoring & redirecting that behavior during their stay.

**My dog is nervous around other dogs / was attacked before.**
Thanks for letting me know! Since I only watch one pup at a time, they won't have to worry about other dogs popping up, and I'll go slow with the introduction to Brownie so they have time to feel comfortable.

**My dog guards food / needs to eat separately.**
No problem, I'll feed them separately from Brownie!

## Meet & greets and booking logistics

**How does the introduction work? Why do you take my dog in alone first?**
My usual process: I'll take your pup inside myself first to do the introduction w Brownie. Once they're comfortable with each other I'll bring them both out to the driveway so u can see how they get along! It usually takes less than 5 min. I do it this way because some dogs act protective in front of their owners at first.

**Where exactly do we meet at the park?**
There's no designated dog area, so we'll just meet by the parking lot & go from there!

**Can we do a trial day care before the stay?**
Definitely! We can set up a trial day care before the stay so your pup gets familiar with me & Brownie.

**What do I need to bring?**
Please bring:
- Food
- water AND food bowls
- leash
- a portioning container (cup, scoop, etc.) or pre-portioned food in zip-loc bags
Everything else is optional! Feel free to bring treats/toys/blankets/a bed if you think it'll make them more comfortable, otherwise I'll provide them.

**What do drop-off & pick-up look like?**
We'll just meet in my driveway! Text me your ETA when you're on the way & I'll come out to meet you. Please don't knock on the door as my dog will go crazy 😂 If you've got a lot of stuff, I have a cart.

**How flexible are you on drop-off & pick-up times?**
Pretty flexible! I just ask for a 30-min window for drop-off & pickup so I can plan around it. If you're flying, send me your flight # and I'll keep an eye on any delays.

**Can I extend the stay or drop off a day early if plans change?**
Yes, I'll have the availability! Just lmk & I'll modify the booking on my end for you to approve.
(If they ask whether it costs more, don't answer - flag it for the human.)

**What are your rates?**
Great question! My rates are all listed on my Rover profile so you can see the exact pricing there.
(Never state a number, discount, or fee - flag any further money question for the human.)

**Can I have your phone number?**
Happy to share it once the booking is confirmed!

**Can I ship food or supplies to your house?**
Yes you can! Ship it to [YOUR ADDRESS] and I'll lyk once it arrives.
